[[SECTION]]
MID: 13e29989163f492a7f83fc99085734ee
UID: DOC-DEPLOYMENT-ANSIBLE-AUTH-RUNTIME-standalone-mcp-oauth-configuration
TITLE: Standalone MCP OAuth configuration

[TEXT]
MID: 670f2498a80963ea1cb04bd1df6ad2c6
STATEMENT: >>>
After owner enrollment, configure `codexia_oauth_mcp_client_ids` and `codexia_oauth_mcp_project_assignments` together for separately approved, registered MCP clients. The IDs are comma-separated. The assignments map each client to a nonempty list of existing PostgreSQL project UUIDs. Owner and introspection clients have distinct IDs. The stage writes both settings to the private runtime snapshot. The API verifies registered clients and existing project assignments at startup. Leave both settings omitted to keep MCP OAuth clients disabled.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
MID: 8c99165b5a5abea76349f1fa068ead7e
UID: DOC-DEPLOYMENT-ANSIBLE-AUTH-RUNTIME-existing-owner-device-loss-recovery
TITLE: Existing owner device-loss recovery

[TEXT]
MID: 9fdd56ad10555bbf86f336ade0506aac
STATEMENT: >>>
Recovery applies only to the exact `CODEXIA_OAUTH_OWNER_SUBJECT` already staged for a healthy Better Auth deployment. Prepare private `bootstrap.env`, `tls.crt`, and `tls.key` files owned by `codexia`, with `bootstrap.env` containing only the dedicated `CODEXIA_AUTH_BOOTSTRAP_ORIGIN=https://<bootstrap-host>:8443`. The setup hostname must be a strict subdomain of the staged production authentication hostname, so the replacement credential remains valid on the production Passkey RP. Open the pinned operator SSH connection and use the service shell described above to run `~/.local/bin/codexia-grant-passkey-recovery --apply <reviewed-full-image-digest>`. This explicit transaction revokes every owner session and every stored OAuth access and refresh grant, including `offline_access`, then prints one ten-minute grant stored by digest. The transaction also writes a durable `codexia_auth.passkey_recovery_audit` record with the owner ID, timestamp, revocation counts, and grant expiry; the one-use grant is never included in that record. The launcher writes the same sanitized event to the system journal under `codexia-passkey-recovery`, without logging the grant. A second grant cannot be issued until the active grant expires.

With the operator SSH forward open, run `~/.local/bin/codexia-recover-passkey --apply <reviewed-full-image-digest>`. Open the dedicated HTTPS setup page, enter the one-time grant, and register a replacement Passkey for the existing owner ID. Close the launcher and SSH forward and remove the temporary bootstrap and TLS files. Sign in again through the normal production login page. Recovery does not create an author, delete or migrate manuscript data, change the configured owner ID, or register OAuth clients.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]
